<title>MEXICO: Mexico crude port Dos Bocas still shut - port.</title>
<headline>Mexico crude port Dos Bocas still shut - port.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico crude port Dos Bocas remained shut as of 1030 local/1630 GMT on Monday because of winds between 25 to 35 kilometers per hour, port captain Jorge Rojano Rodriguez told Reuters.</p>
<p>The Tabasco state port along the Gulf of Mexico was shut since 1730 local/2330 GMT on Sunday.</p>
<p>Winds velocities appeared to be slowing and the port could reopen later in the day, Rojano said.</p>
<p>--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 7903</p>
